<title>TURKEY: Turkish money/forex/bond report.</title>
<headline>Turkish money/forex/bond report.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkish markets were closed for the Moslem Eid al-Adha holiday on Friday.</p>
<p>Financial and capital markets will open on April 24.</p>
<p>Overnight money rates at Thursday's close -- at midday due to the holiday -- were an average 69.93 percent.</p>
<p>Bond market volume was extremely low in pre-holiday trade and yields were around 94.5 percent at Thursday's close.</p>
<p>The Turkish lira weakened to 132,600 versus the dollar from 132,460 at Wednesday's close.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
